      "exact_reserve_text": "The prior accident year loss ratio is 0.7% better than 2021 at 4.7% and is being driven by a deterioration on named large and catastrophe events including 2021 Malaysian Floods (December), 2019 Ethiopian Airlines loss, 2021 European Floods and 2020 Chesapeake Energy. The 2022 income statement impact for these events is a gross loss impact of GBP 10.9m, GBP 14.0m, GBP 8.9m and GBP 22.7m respectively, and a net deterioration of GBP 9.1m, GBP 6.0m, GBP 5.1m and GBP 4.5m respectively. The impact to the Syndicate result across these events was a gross loss impact of GBP 56.5m and net loss of GBP 24.7m, representing 2.7% of the prior accident year loss ratio of 4.7%. The profit on the technical account of GBP 9.7m (2021: profit GBP 54.5m) includes a run-off deficit of GBP 43.9m for prior accident years (2021: GBP 32.2m deficit). This included a deficit of GBP 40.4m for reinsurance acceptance business and a deficit of GBP 3.5m on direct business (2021: deficit of GBP 23.1m for reinsurance acceptance business and a deficit of GBP 9.1m on direct business).",
