      "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 1414 experienced a net prior-year reserve strengthening for older accident years in 2022. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle shows an aggregate gross adverse development of approximately GBP 94.7m across underwriting years 2013-2020 (excluding 2021 and 2022). The movement was driven primarily by deterioration on a number of prior large losses and catastrophe events (notably 2019 Ethiopian Airlines, 2021 Malaysian and European floods and 2020 Chesapeake Energy) combined with continued claims inflation and increased frequency/severity. The managing agent also reports a run-off deficit on prior accident years in its technical note (stated as GBP 43.9m run-off deficit on prior years in the technical account narrative, which is a different/net measure). Reinsurance accepted business accounted for the majority of the prior year deterioration as reported.",
